# drive v1: mctas mobfarm siding-bench <design> --wired --launch --from 1 --to 1 --nights 1 --placed-raw --drive-out F (arrivals launched from rest on the bench's launcher; the release placed as a block: the loop's input)
# caption carts launched in and released by the test bench; the siding's own redstone does the rest
# seed 1
# days 2
# walk random
# ai on
# start Run::start(spec, RunOpts { ai: true, raw: true, ..RunOpts::steady(seed, days * 24000, WalkMode::Random) }) (the file pasted as written, no settle); the design's entity lines spawned in order (eN: line N from 0, eN.pK: its passenger K from 0); t0 = the world's time then
# act t: applied when the world's time is t0 + t, before the run's next tick (the bench's own order)
# t0 0
# placed: settled as placed: Run::start(spec, RunOpts { raw: true, .. }): the design's blocks written raw, its nbt: lines merged (the game's data merge), no shape or neighbour update and no settle (the Nether part too); the entities spawned at once (t0 = the world's time then)
# expect t: the event happened in the tick that brought the world's time to t0 + t (an act at t comes before the tick to t0 + t + 1)
